<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc235450353" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 2 — Bold used for a UI element inside a procedure</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a procedural step that reads: "Click the Save button." The word "Save" is wrapped</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>element</keyword>
        <keyword>inside</keyword>
        <keyword>Save</keyword>
        <keyword>button</keyword>
        <keyword>strong</keyword>
        <keyword>Click</keyword>
        <indexterm>element</indexterm>
        <indexterm>inside</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Save</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
    <p>Consider a procedural step that reads: "Click the <b>Save</b> button." The word "Save" is wrapped in <codeph>&lt;strong&gt;</codeph> because it represents a UI button label.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Strong used for UI element</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;ol>
    &lt;li>
        Click the &lt;strong>Save&lt;/strong> button.
    &lt;/li>
&lt;/ol></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;taskbody>
  &lt;steps>
    &lt;step>
      &lt;cmd>
        Click the &lt;uicontrol>Save&lt;/uicontrol> button.
      &lt;/cmd>
    &lt;/step>
  &lt;/steps>
&lt;/taskbody></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
         <p><b>Result:</b> The converter recognizes that the <codeph>&lt;strong&gt;</codeph> element represents a UI label within a procedural step and maps it to <codeph>&lt;uicontrol&gt;</codeph> instead of <codeph>&lt;b&gt;</codeph>. A <codeph>&lt;strong&gt;</codeph> element inside an <codeph>&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;</codeph> within a task topic is treated as a UI label and mapped to <codeph>&lt;uicontrol&gt;</codeph>. The same <codeph>&lt;strong&gt;</codeph> element inside a descriptive <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> in a concept topic would be mapped to <codeph>&lt;b&gt;</codeph>.</p>
  </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
